Subject: [PATCH 10652/11362] Measure the rate: the self-served substrate list
 grew 21 to 23 in six hours

Follow-up to the 10:38Z finding, which established that every entry in
DETERMINISTIC_VERIFIER_SUBSTRATES was added by the artifact seeking the exemption
but could not say how fast that was happening. It is two per six hours at the
current cadence: exp6843 added read_only_live_artifact_inventory and exp6844 added
deterministic_cpu_live_receipt_audit_no_llm, each in the same commit as its own
artifact, verified with git show --name-only rather than --stat, which truncates
paths and produced a wrong answer the first time.

The counter-example is recorded alongside the rate because it changes what a fix
should look like. exp6849 declared "deterministic CPU exact compilation", drew the
SUBSTRATE_HAS_NO_DURATION_FLOOR warn, and did not add its string. Its artifact
carries the warn honestly. So this is a channel some tasks use and others decline,
not a universal behaviour, and any lint written against it must expect legitimate
warns to persist rather than treating a warn as a defect to be cleared.

